// A completion-based outbound byte budget.
//
// Permit an outbound HTTP request while delivered request bytes recorded in
// `http:request::response` history during the last 60 seconds total less than 100.
// The gateway records the outcome when the exchange ends, including completion,
// failure, or timeout. The window uses recording time, not physical delivery time.
//
// Pending exchanges do not count yet, so stalled or concurrent exchanges can exceed
// the threshold. The rule also permits the next request without adding its size to
// the recorded total, so that request can exceed the threshold.
//
// Sum `::response` events, never `::request` ones: a request's `body_bytes` is what
// the workload offered, while an outcome reports request bytes known to have reached
// the operating system. A denied attempt does not consume this budget.
//
// `formerly within 60s` bounds the window and the engine's retained state.
@id("egress_byte_budget")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Box::Action::"http:request",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (total: Long). (
        (sum b for (b: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (
            formerly within 60s (
                Box::Action::"http:request"::response{ input.host: _, input.body_bytes: b } && tp(t)
            )
        )) == total
        && total < 100
    )
};
